<DocsLayout title="Architecture">
  <h1>Architecture</h1>
  <p>
    Identity is a stateless Connect-RPC server. All durable state lives in
    EntDB. The container does five things on startup, then serves requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Process layout</h2>
  <Code code={`Browser / SDK
     |
     |  Connect-RPC over HTTP/JSON  (port 80)
     v
+-------------------------------+        +--------+
| Identity container            | -----> |        |
|                               |        |        |
|  Logging  -> CORS -> Health   |        | EntDB  |
|     -> JWKS  -> Auth          |        |        |
|     -> service.IdentityHandler|        |        |
+-------------------------------+        +--------+
     |
     |  Prometheus  (port 9090)
     v
  /metrics`} lang="plaintext" />

  <h2>Layers</h2>
  <p>
    Concrete files live under <code>internal/</code> and <code>pkg/</code>.
    Each layer has a single responsibility:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>cmd/identity/main.go</code> — process bootstrap, key-ring loading, middleware chain, graceful shutdown.</li>
    <li><code>internal/middleware/</code> — logging, CORS, health, JWKS endpoint, bearer-token auth.</li>
    <li><code>internal/connect/</code> — Connect-RPC adapter that translates between proto types and the service-layer Go types.</li>
    <li><code>internal/service/</code> — business logic. <code>AuthService</code>, <code>AdminService</code>, <code>GroupService</code>, <code>HelpService</code>, <code>ProfileService</code>. None of these import Connect or proto types.</li>
    <li><code>internal/repo</code> — three backends behind the <code>service.Repository</code> / <code>service.DB</code> interfaces, picked by <code>GATEWAY_BACKEND</code>: <code>memory</code> (dev / tests), <code>postgres</code>, and <code>entdb</code> (production default, multi-tenant via tenant-shard-db). The <code>conformance</code> sub-package runs the same suite of behavioural tests against every backend so semantics (uniqueness, ordering, error translation) don't drift.</li>
    <li><code>internal/repo/entdb/entclient</code> — the only place that calls <code>sdk.NewClient</code>. Wraps it with <code>sdk.WithSchema(...)</code> pre-filled by <code>SchemaMessages()</code> so every node/edge type in <code>proto/identity/schema/schema.proto</code> is attached on the first <code>ExecuteAtomic</code> per tenant (ADR-031 self-describing writes). The server materialises the registry — type ids, field options, composite-unique indexes — before the data ops, so field types, single- and composite-unique constraints, and required-fields are enforced atomically.</li>
    <li><code>pkg/jwt</code> — <code>KeyRing</code>, <code>SigningKey</code>, <code>CreateAccessToken</code>, <code>VerifyAccessToken</code>, JWKS marshalling.</li>
    <li><code>pkg/passwords</code> — bcrypt hashing (cost 12) + a strength validator.</li>
    <li><code>pkg/passkeys</code> — WebAuthn (<code>go-webauthn/webauthn</code>) wrapper.</li>
    <li><code>pkg/totp</code> — RFC 6238 TOTP + AES-GCM encryption for secrets at rest.</li>
    <li><code>pkg/audit</code> — append-only logger that writes <code>AuditEvent</code> nodes to EntDB.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Middleware chain</h2>
  <p>
    The chain is built in <code>cmd/identity/main.go</code>. Outermost runs
    first on the request path:
  </p>
  <Code code={`logging -> CORS -> health -> JWKS -> auth -> Connect handler`} lang="plaintext" />
  <ul>
    <li><strong>logging</strong> — structured zap logs with request ID, latency, status.</li>
    <li><strong>CORS</strong> — comma-separated origins from <code>GATEWAY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>health</strong> — answers <code>/health</code> and <code>/healthz</code> before reaching the auth layer.</li>
    <li><strong>JWKS</strong> — serves <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code> straight from the in-memory <code>KeyRing</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>auth</strong> — verifies bearer tokens and writes the user ID to <code>X-Authenticated-User-Id</code>. Skipped for the exempt-path list (signup, login, JWKS, health, etc.).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Graceful shutdown</h2>
  <p>
    On <code>SIGTERM</code> or <code>SIGINT</code>, the server stops accepting
    new connections, waits up to 10 seconds for in-flight RPCs, then closes
    the EntDB client. The metrics server runs in its own goroutine and is
    cleaned up by process exit.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
